{"agent":"fleet-docs-a","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`_parsed` short-circuits on `_MARK in text`, i.e. it skips `RG.parse` entirely whenever the literal substring `ddflow:begin` does not occur, and returns `[]` — which is exactly the \"no regions, nothing to report\" answer rather than the \"markers unreadable\" answer. So a hand-edit that removes the begin marker line (`<!-- ddflow:begin doc/page <hash> -->`) while leaving the matching `<!-- ddflow:end doc/page -->` in place — a common botched merge-conflict resolution — turns into silence: `problem()` returns `\"\"` and `edited()` returns `[]`, so the pre-commit check and the doctor note both read the file as a clean whole-file document and let it through. An orphaned end marker is the textbook \"unbalanced\" marker case the module docstring promises is reported by `problem`, and the body hash can no longer be checked at all once the begin marker is gone. `mask()` has the same hop (it returns `_parsed()`, so a `RegionError` path is never reached here either), leaving the leftover template lines in the text docscheck prose-checks. The guard should only elide the no-marker-at-all case (which `RG.parse` already answers with `[]`); as written it also elides the malformed case.","digest":"b687e74abf20edb6","location":"ddflow/services/export/region_check.py:19 (`_parsed`)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/export/region_check.py:19 (`_parsed`)"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"3/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":14507,"diff_sha":"ef6bdd00bc818ae40636bd877d61bbb31b9fe77f2feeb652c13a3bd34d8be1c6","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1800.1,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"cf827af452e1996d","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/B-tpl